      <div class="blog-body">
        <h2>Why HMO Landlords Face Stricter Gas Safety Rules</h2>
        <p>An HMO has more people in it than a family let. More people use the gas. Shared appliances often belong to no one tenant. All of this raises the risk. So Liverpool City Council makes gas safety part of its HMO licence rules.</p>
        <p>Liverpool has a lot of HMOs, in part because of its large student population. The council's housing team can inspect HMOs. It can also ask to see your gas safety certificate.</p>
        <CallStrip inline title="Got a plumbing problem now?" text="A real person answers 24/7. No call-out fee." />

        <h2>What Is an HMO in Liverpool?</h2>
        <p>Under the Housing Act 2004, a home is an HMO if three or more people from two or more households live there. They must also share a kitchen, bathroom or toilet. You need a mandatory licence from <a href="https://liverpool.gov.uk/housing/private-rented-accommodation/multiple-occupancy-homes/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Liverpool City Council</a> if five or more people from two or more households live there. The council may also run extra licensing schemes in some areas. These can cover smaller HMOs too.</p>

        <div class="blog-callout">
          <strong>Check if your property needs an extra licence</strong>
          <p>In some parts of the city, the council may need you to license homes that would not need a mandatory licence. Check the <a href="https://liverpool.gov.uk/housing/private-rented-accommodation/multiple-occupancy-homes/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Liverpool City Council HMO licensing pages</a> to see if your home is covered.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>Gas Safety Certificate Requirements for Liverpool HMOs</h2>
        <p>The gas safety law for HMOs is the same as for any let. It is the <a href="https://www.hse.gov.uk/gas/landlords/index.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gas Safety (Installation and Use) Regulations 1998</a>. But in an HMO, getting it wrong costs more:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Giving the council a valid gas safety certificate when asked is a licence condition</li>
          <li>The council can act against your licence if you break its conditions, such as letting the certificate lapse</li>
          <li>Running an HMO without a licence you need is a criminal offence. You face an unlimited fine and could be told to pay back rent</li>
          <li>Failing to get a yearly gas safety check is also a criminal offence. The <a href="https://www.hse.gov.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Health and Safety Executive</a> can prosecute</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What the CP12 Must Cover in an HMO Property</h2>
        <p>Every gas appliance you provide must be checked. It does not matter if it is in a shared space or a tenant's room. This includes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The gas boiler</li>
          <li>Gas fires in shared areas or in rooms</li>
          <li>Gas hobs in shared kitchens</li>
          <li>Any other gas appliance you provide in a tenant's room</li>
          <li>All gas pipework you can see and reach</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Some HMOs have more than one boiler, for example one on each floor. Each boiler must be checked and included.</p>
        <p>We cover boilers, gas cookers and hobs. Got a gas fire? Tell us when you book. If you no longer need it, we can disconnect and cap it safely, so it no longer has to be on the certificate. If you want to keep using it, it must be checked by an engineer registered for gas fires.</p>

        <h2>Carbon Monoxide Alarms in Liverpool HMOs</h2>
        <p>Since October 2022, landlords in England must fit a carbon monoxide alarm in any room with a fixed appliance that burns fuel. Gas cookers do not count. So in an HMO with gas appliances in many rooms, each of those rooms needs an alarm. Alarms must work on the day each new tenancy starts.</p>
        <p>If you break the alarm rules, the council can fine you up to £5,000.</p>

        <h2>Managing Gas Safety Across Multiple HMOs in Liverpool</h2>
        <p>With several HMOs, it is easy to lose track of dates. We make it simple:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A free renewal reminder for each property</li>
          <li>All certificates emailed the same day as the check</li>
          <li>£100 for up to two appliances, usually the boiler and hob, plus £20 for each extra appliance after two</li>
          <li>£80 per property if you have 3 or more properties</li>
          <li>Gas safety check and boiler service together for £199</li>
        </ul>
        <p>All prices include VAT.</p>

        <h2>What Happens If a Gas Safety Issue Is Found During an HMO Inspection?</h2>
        <p>We follow the <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gas Industry Unsafe Situations Procedure</a> on every check. If an appliance is Immediately Dangerous, we make it safe before we leave. You get a written report and a repair price before we do any more work. We give you a written warning notice for anything unsafe, as the procedure requires.</p>
        <p>We cannot issue a certificate until all Immediately Dangerous faults are put right. If your licence renewal is close, call us on <a href="tel:01515580334">0151 558 0334</a> as soon as you can.</p>
        <CallStrip inline title="Want us to take a look?" text="Call for advice or a price. Gas Safe registered, no call-out fee." />

        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="pf-faq">
          <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">LICENCE</span><span class="pf-faq-q">Do I need a CP12 to get an HMO licence in Liverpool?</span></summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Giving the council a valid gas safety certificate when asked is a condition of an HMO licence. The certificate must cover every gas appliance you provide. You must renew it every 12 months.</p></div></details>
          <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">MULTIPLE</span><span class="pf-faq-q">My HMO has multiple boilers. Does each need its own certificate?</span></summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Every gas appliance must be covered. If there are several boilers, we check them all. We check every boiler, gas cooker and hob in one visit and email the certificate the same day. We do not check gas fires. A gas fire must be checked by an engineer registered for gas fires, or we can disconnect and cap it safely.</p></div></details>
          <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">LAPSE</span><span class="pf-faq-q">What happens if my CP12 lapses during my HMO licence period?</span></summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Missing a yearly gas safety check is a criminal offence. It also breaks your licence conditions, and the council can act against your licence. Running an HMO without a licence you need carries an unlimited fine. If your certificate has lapsed, call us on <a href="tel:01515580334">0151 558 0334</a> straight away.</p></div></details>
          <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">PORTFOLIO</span><span class="pf-faq-q">Do you offer portfolio rates for multiple Liverpool HMOs?</span></summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Book 3 or more properties and each certificate is £80. Certificates are emailed the same day. Call <a href="tel:01515580334">0151 558 0334</a> to talk about your portfolio.</p></div></details>
          <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">CO ALARM</span><span class="pf-faq-q">Are CO alarms required in Liverpool HMOs?</span></summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Since October 2022, landlords in England must fit a CO alarm in any room with a fixed appliance that burns fuel. Gas cookers do not count. In an HMO, that can mean an alarm in many rooms. The council can fine you up to £5,000 if you do not comply.</p></div></details>
        </div>
      </div>

